// RigSpec v1 (Cyrus R3 creature pipeline): what the build model writes in assets/creatures/<name>.json and what Nxeon's
// compiler (./compile.ts) turns into a Blockbench .bbmodel for the Nxeon-managed BetterModel plugin, a skin PNG and
// baked keyframe animations. The model never writes .bbmodel JSON, UUIDs, UV rectangles or keyframe maths itself.
// Pure + client-safe (Zod + plain TS). The build service's copy (services/modbuilder/creature-spec.js) is GENERATED
// from this file by scripts/cyrus/build-creature-artifacts.ts; test/cyrus-creature.test.ts checks it is current and
// gives the same answer on every fixture. The JSON Schema contract is ./rigspec.v1.schema.json (same script).
//
// Two forms, one schema:
//   template form  { version, name, archetype, template: { features?, height? }, skin: { palette }, sounds, ... }
//                  -> bones + animations come from Nxeon's archetype template (./templates.ts): the reliable path.
//   explicit form  { version, name, archetype, bones: [...], animations: {...}, skin, sounds, ... }
//                  -> for shapes no template covers (still validated against every limit below).
